ergy  price package which was only funded by  borrowing not a windfall tax because  there was surprising Labor's taking  notorious for fiscal irresponsibility  and then we saw that added to in the  budget that quasi-karting produced on  the subject of energy which obviously is  your brain you're talking about fracking  today you've been very critical of the  government's plan to lift the ban on  fracking so what are you going to do  about it well we are going to do  everything we can through the House of  Commons and there is support across the  House of Commons for for carrying on  with the ban on fracking uh to try and  force the government to change its mind  why is fracking not the answer first of  all it will make no difference to gas  prices because where the gas is produced  here or produced internationally we pay  the same price for it secondly the  government gave a categorical Assurance  in their Manifesto they said we are not  going to restart fracking unless it can  be categorically shown to be safe and  and they haven't got the evidence and  they're and they're breaking since then  Russia has invaded Ukraine that's had a  massive impact on Energy prices and they  say that it's in the National interest  to reintroduce them more extreme Fringe  views from a government that is of the  extreme Fringe of the conservative party  look Boris Johnson opposed fracking  quasi quatting themselves it a few  months ago fracking will make no  difference to Energy prices much better  stop it well much better to go ahead  with Labor's plans for a clean energy  Sprint for zero carbon power system by  2030. for example the government is also  talking about blocking solar energy the  equivalent of 10 nuclear power stations  worth of solar energy that's completely  wrong solar energy is the cheapest form  of power that we have how do we stop it  we'll do everything we can to work with  MPS from across parties conservative MPS  I'm talking to some conservative MPS we  I will do everything we can to try and  stop this how many Tory MPS are prepared  to go against the government well I I  don't know the answer to that but I know  there is a lot of disquiet from talking  to conservative MPS about this we'll we  will find a way of testing opinion in  the House of Commons you know we get  opposition days and we're thinking about  how we can use at that time uh to have  uh votes on fracking but we do want to  stop this and you know the other thing  is uh and and you know it's so clear  clear to me that people in the country  don't want fracking it's the least  popular form of energy that they that  they can be but the government says  they'll only go ahead if they have local  concerns well they don't quite say that  Liz trusted that during her leadership  campaign that they haven't they she  cannot say what local consent even means  and there is a fear that they can  actually bypass local people when it  comes to fracking that will be quite  wrong and on the subject of of sonar  Farms this trust did say she'd block  them on agricultural land during her  leadership campaign but her argument  would be wouldn't it that they we need  to boost food production at a time when  food prices are soaring and we can't  afford to import them and the biggest  threat to food security is the climate  crisis and you know how much because  listro has sort of made much of this  fact that solar Farms apparently  destroying all that Farmland do you know  how much Farmland is actually being used  by solar panels at the moment 0.1  percent one one thousandth of of uh  farmland and even if we increase solar  panels by five times it would be only  half a percent of Farmland I'm afraid  it's you see there is a piece of this  with with what we saw in the budget  we've got a party that has got dangerous  extreme views essentially taken over the  conservative party and is now trying to  impose those views on the country and it  is bad for the country it's the wrong  priorities for Britain I asked this  question to Greg hands do you expect um  to be in office in a month's time I have  absolutely no idea but you know what if  the conservative party seems really  worried about the trashing of the  conservative party I'm worried about the  trashing of the country I'm worried  about people's mortgages I'm worried  about the the spectacle the the impact  this is having on people across Britain  and I honestly believe that the whole of  the conservative party Bears  responsibility for this they elected Liz  truss they they impose yet another prime  minister uh on us you know I feel like  they're gambles at the casino they bet  the house on one prime minister then  they get rid of them and they bet the  house on another prime minister there's  only one answer for this which is the  conservative budget get out of the way  and let a labor government govern the  country okay Ed mediban thanks very much  thank you

